  "body": "## Goal\n\nStep 1, PR E of the UI plan #4245. All user commands of the shell come from one command table. The ribbon reads that table (no second list), and a new in-app menu bar (File, Edit, View, Setup, Operation, Tools, Help, or the groups the table gives) also reads it. Each entry has its label, its icon, its hover text, its shortcut and its enabled rule with the reason when it is disabled.\n\n## What is decided (#4245, maintainer answers)\n\n- The app gets a menu bar, as users know from other desktop programs.\n- A native macOS menu bar needs a new dependency, so it is a later follow-up for the maintainer (not this PR).\n- A command search comes after this PR (a P7 follow-up).\n- PR R (#4398) split `panes.rs`: `panes/cmd.rs` (the `Cmd` type, the group plan, labels, text, hover text), `panes/gates.rs` (enabled rules, create gates, routes, icons) and `panes/run.rs` (run a command). Start from these files.\n\n## Scope\n\n- One table: each command is one row with its id, label, icon, hover text, shortcut, menu group, ribbon group and enabled rule. The ribbon and the menu bar both render from it. A command never has two labels.\n- Every command still goes through the undoable command path of the app (AGENTS.md \"Everything Is a Command\"). The menu bar adds no new state change.\n- Shortcuts: one place to declare them. A test refuses two commands with the same shortcut.\n- Disabled entries show the reason in the hover text (the existing gates).\n\n## Done means\n\n- The menu bar shows every command of the ribbon. A test checks that the ribbon and the menu bar list the same command ids from the table.\n- A test checks that each command id has a label, a hover text and an enabled rule, and that no two commands share a shortcut.\n- The ribbon looks the same as before (structural and layout tests). The new menu bar has its own layout test (`layout_window_*` or `layout_page_*`). The `crates/ui` test count does not go down (#1953). No snapshot PNG changes.\n- Before and after screenshots at 1366×768.\n- No change to toolpaths, posts or the project file.\n\nPart of #4245. Enables PR D (title bar, workflow tabs) and PR F (#3025, Settings window).\n",
